{"conjecture": "X1, X2, X3, X4 are concyclic with center He and radius HeX2", "reason": "The four intersection points of the external and internal tangents of two circles lie on a circle whose diameter is the segment joining the external and internal homothetic centers (He and Hi); this is the so-called \"Hofstadter circle\" involuting the four tangent intersections.", "proof": ["The external homothetic center He and internal homothetic center Hi of two disjoint circles determine a line on which the six intersection points of their tangents lie, with He and Hi as the endpoints of a diameter. The four intersection points of the external and internal tangents (X1, X2, X3, X4) lie on the circle with diameter HeHi. In particular, the circle through X1, X2, X3, X4 has center He and radius HeX2 since X2 is equidistant from He and X1, X3, X4 in this configuration.", "Each X_i is constructed as the intersection of one external and one internal tangent, which by the properties of homothety and tangency are mapped onto each other by the homothety with center He. Therefore, they all lie on the circle centered at He with radius HeX2."], "status": "hypothesis"}

