{"conjecture": "X1, X2, X3, X4 are concyclic, with He as the center and HiX3 as the diameter.", "proof": "1. In the configuration, the external tangents of the two circles intersect at He, and the internal tangents intersect at Hi. 2. The polar of Hi with respect to each circle passes through He, making He the pole of the line HiX3. 3. Hence the four intersection points X1, X2, X3, X4 lie on the circle with center He and diameter HiX3.", "status": "hypothesis", "closes_goal": true}

